{#
    The page every rendered document is written into.

    It shadows the same path in phpDocumentor's default theme, which produces
    a bare document with no way to leave it. The navigation is built here from
    `allDocuments` rather than from a toctree, because a toctree is a
    reStructuredText directive and this corpus is markdown.

    What the renderer leaves to a theme is more than the layout: there is no
    search, no highlighting of a fenced block whose language it has just
    written into the markup, and no way to copy one. All three come from
    `assets/site.js`, which is where each says what it costs.

    Every icon in the chrome is `<sds-icon>`. The element says where its sprite
    is and what a glyph is called, and nothing here draws one — the signet is
    the exception, inlined because it is this site's own drawing and carries two
    colours the page sets rather than one it inherits.

    Each says `size="16"`. An icon is as big as the text it sits in by default,
    which is right for a glyph inside a label and wrong for these: a fold
    marker beside an 11px section label is an affordance, not a word, and at
    11px it is a smudge. 16 is the floor the system sets for a glyph standing
    on its own, and every one of these stands on its own.

    The stylesheet and the script are two files rather than two blocks in every
    page: at 16 KB they had grown to a third of everything this site serves.
    What that costs is `D-DOC-019`.
#}
{% set here = env.currentFileName %}
{% set depth = here|split('/')|length - 1 %}
{% set up = '' %}
{% if depth > 0 %}{% for i in 1..depth %}{% set up = up ~ '../' %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{#
    Three runs, in the order somebody arrives in: the front page, then the
    pages that belong to no subject, then each subject with its own heading.
    Sorted by the path alone, a loose page lands between two directories and
    reads as part of whichever one it fell into.
#}
{% set pages = env.allDocuments|sort((a, b) =>
    ((a.filePath|trim('/') == 'index' ? '0' : (a.filePath matches '#/#' ? '2' : '1')) ~ a.filePath|trim('/'))
    <=>
    ((b.filePath|trim('/') == 'index' ? '0' : (b.filePath matches '#/#' ? '2' : '1')) ~ b.filePath|trim('/'))
) %}
{#
    What the three built assets are called this build, read out of the
    manifest `assets/build.mjs` writes, in the order it writes them:
    stylesheet, script, icon sprite. Each name carries a hash of the file, so a
    changed asset is a changed URL and an unchanged one is never asked about
    again.
#}
{% set assets = source('assets/dist/manifest.txt')|trim|split('\n') %}
{% set mark = (env.projectNode.title ?? 'Documentation')|split(' ', 2) %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-up="{{ up }}" data-sprite="{{ up }}assets/{{ assets[2] }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ title }}
        {%- if title != null and env.projectNode.title != null %} — {% endif -%}
        {%- if env.projectNode.title -%}{{ env.projectNode.title }}{%- endif -%}</title>
    {# The signet is redrawn per optical size rather than scaled; this is the one for 16–19px. #}
    <link rel="icon" href="{{ up }}assets/signet-s.svg" sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml">
    {#
        The two faces every page sets before anything else is read. Without
        this the wordmark is laid out in the fallback and re-laid out when the
        face arrives — a jump on every navigation, because each document runs
        its own font loading whatever the cache holds.
    #}
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ up }}assets/source-sans-3-latin-400-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ up }}assets/source-sans-3-latin-600-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ up }}assets/{{ assets[0] }}">
    {#
        The one thing that runs before the page is painted, because a reader who
        chose a mode is otherwise shown the other one for a frame. Everything
        else this theme runs is the deferred file.
    #}
    <script>var t=localStorage.getItem('theme');if(t){document.documentElement.dataset.theme=t;}</script>
    {%~ block head %}
    {%~ endblock %}
</head>
<body>
<header class="top">
    <div class="bar">
        {#
            Shown by the script and on a narrow screen alone. Written hidden so
            that a reader without JavaScript keeps the list rather than a button
            that cannot open it.
        #}
        <button id="menu" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="side" aria-label="Pages" hidden><sds-icon name="actions-list" size="16"></sds-icon></button>
        <a class="lockup" href="{{ up }}index.html">
            <span class="signet">{{ source('assets/icons/signet-m.svg')|raw }}</span>
            <span class="wordmark">
                <span>{{ mark[0] }}</span>
                {%- if mark[1] is defined %}<span class="wordmark__pipe" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="wordmark__product">{{ mark[1] }}</span>{% endif -%}
            </span>
        </a>
        {#
            The same: a button that opens the search, shown by the script alone,
            because a field that searches nothing is worse than no field.
        #}
        <button id="find" class="find" type="button" aria-keyshortcuts="Control+K" hidden>
            <sds-icon name="actions-search" size="16"></sds-icon>
            <span>Search</span><kbd id="key">Ctrl K</kbd>
        </button>
        {#
            Two segments, and the mode a reader has not chosen is the machine's.
            Shown by the script, since nothing else can change it.
        #}
        <div class="modes" id="modes" role="group" aria-label="Colour mode" hidden>
            <button type="button" data-mode="light" aria-pressed="false">light</button>
            <button type="button" data-mode="dark" aria-pressed="false">dark</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</header>
{#
    The search is a dialog and no longer a list written into the sidebar: what
    a reader searches for is a page, and the sidebar is the list of pages they
    were already looking past — on a narrow screen it is folded away entirely,
    so the hits were written where nobody could see them.

    `showModal()` carries the focus, the backdrop and the escape key, so none
    of the three is written here.
#}
<dialog id="search" aria-label="Search the documentation">
    <div class="field">
        <sds-icon name="actions-search" size="16"></sds-icon>
        <input id="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search the documentation" aria-label="Search the documentation" aria-controls="hits">
    </div>
    <ul id="hits"></ul>
    <p id="miss" hidden>Nothing carries that.</p>
    <p id="rest">Type to search {{ pages|length }} pages.</p>
    {# Named rather than drawn: the return glyph is outside the subsets these
       two families ship, so it arrives as a box on a machine whose fallback
       mono has no better idea. #}
    <footer><kbd>&#8593;</kbd><kbd>&#8595;</kbd> move <kbd>enter</kbd> open <kbd>esc</kbd> close</footer>
</dialog>
{#
    A drawing is 1200px wide and the column is 800. This is where it is read at
    the size it was drawn at, and on a narrow screen it is the only place it can
    be read at all — the panel scrolls rather than shrinking the drawing again.
#}
<dialog id="zoom">
    <div class="zoom__head">
        <p id="zoom-said"></p>
        <button type="button" class="zoom__close" aria-label="Close"><sds-icon name="actions-close" size="16"></sds-icon></button>
    </div>
    {# Filled with the drawing being read, which the script has already inlined. #}
    <div class="zoom__body"></div>
</dialog>
<div class="wrap">
    <nav class="side sds-rail" id="side">
        {#
            The system's rail, written as its classes rather than as
            `<sds-rail>`: this is the navigation of the page, and it has to be
            there before a script is. The element and the classes emit the same
            markup — that is the contract — so this is the same rail, rendered
            by the renderer that has the list of pages.

            The front page and the pages belonging to no subject stand open;
            every subject is a fold, and the one being read is the one that
            starts open.
        #}
        {%- for entry in pages|filter(entry => (entry.filePath|trim('/') matches '#/#') == false) -%}
            {%- set path = entry.filePath|trim('/') -%}
            <a class="sds-rail__item{{ path == here ? ' is-active' : '' }}" href="{{ up }}{{ path }}.html"{{ path == here ? ' aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ path == 'index' ? 'Overview' : (entry.title ? entry.title.toString : path) }}</a>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- set group = '' -%}
        {%- for entry in pages|filter(entry => entry.filePath|trim('/') matches '#/#') -%}
            {%- set path = entry.filePath|trim('/') -%}
            {%- set dir = path|split('/')|first -%}
            {%- if dir != group -%}
                {%- if group != '' %}</details>{% endif -%}
                {%- set group = dir -%}
                <details class="sds-rail__group"{{ here|split('/')|first == dir ? ' open' : '' }}>
                    <summary><sds-icon name="actions-chevron-down" size="16"></sds-icon>{{ dir|replace({'-': ' '}) }}</summary>
            {%- endif -%}
            <a class="sds-rail__item{{ path == here ? ' is-active' : '' }}" href="{{ up }}{{ path }}.html"{{ path == here ? ' aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ entry.title ? entry.title.toString : path }}</a>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- if group != '' %}</details>{% endif -%}
    </nav>
    <main>
<!-- content start -->
{%~ block body %}
{%~ endblock %}
<!-- content end -->
    </main>
</div>
<script src="{{ up }}assets/{{ assets[1] }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
